{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgLmaLcuxd5Wrub7uQRMG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking for a build plan for a 375×812 crypto wallet flow. The open unknowns are: which fonts actually load (Nunito Regular, Medium, SemiBold, Bold, ExtraBold, plus Inter Semi Bold for the status bar, all via figma.loadFontAsync), whether I have write permission on the file, and whether the coin logo components carry image fills whose hash survives cloning. So the first substantive step is one call that lists available font families and styles, reads the fills on the Coin_BTC component to confirm an IMAGE paint, inspects the layout alignment fields of the existing Button component, and creates then removes a small frame as a write test. That call is read-side mostly, so it is safe to run before anything else.\n\nThen the build itself. Canvas 6 at 375×812 with a 44 status bar and a 34 home indicator gives 734 usable. For 01_Wallet I allocate: header 60, dark graphite balance card 136 (rounded 24, white 34px figure 54,292.79, lime +5.21% pill), actions row 60 (Send/Receive), assets header plus 4 rows at 50 each, pockets header plus 3 horizontal cards at 96 each (two pockets and a dashed Add Pocket). That lands at roughly 712 with the nav starting around 722, so it fits without clipping.\n\n02_Discovery genuinely does not fit: 10 coin rows alone at 40px are 400, and with search, tabs, For You cards and 4 strategy cards the total is about 944. So 01, 02 and 03 get VERTICAL_SCROLLING on the content column, which the brief permits. I order Discovery as search, tabs, For You, strategies, coins, and keep everything present in the node tree rather than dropped.\n\nMedia handling: clone the coin components into a Media section on the workspace page so image fills live there, then instance them locally. Cloning copies the image hash, so the logos stay real images, not redrawn vectors.\n\n03_Strategy, 04_Invest_Amount and 05_Invest_Success are sheets sitting on a dimmed clone of the Discovery content, so the layer beneath reads as the same screen. Each sheet has a scrolling body and a pinned Invest or Hold to Invest footer.\n\nColours: ink 2B2D33, secondary 6B6F80, border EBECF2, gain 12A66B, loss E5484D, risk high F04E3E on FEECE9, medium E39B12 on FEF4E2, low 12A66B on E7F7F0.\n\nI request the font-and-write-test call now; it depends on nothing.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":7524,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":24263,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7524}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7fa41065-9ea8-4467-818a-aa7f032bdf86","uuid":"29074784-172f-40d7-ad30-c300bbdd4dce","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:34:09.164Z","thinking_duration_ms":74282}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgLmaLcuxd5Wrub7uQRMG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have the brief, foundations, component and media structure. Before building I need three things: which exact font styles exist, whether I can write to the workspace page, and how the coin logos and Button are constructed. All three are independent, so I'm checking them in one call."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":7524,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":24263,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7524}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7fa41065-9ea8-4467-818a-aa7f032bdf86","uuid":"48ed23ef-eae9-4657-80f5-f575516224ab","timestamp":"2026-10-31T19:34:10.878Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgLmaLcuxd5Wrub7uQRMG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01uOtYo8GlpinUBgcoposVCG","name":"mcp__figma__use_figma","input":{"fileKey":"DahEt2glvB09pBFT66GiDO","description":"Read-only inspection: available Nunito/Inter font styles, coin logo image fills, Button alignment, plus a small write-permission test on the empty 03 Workspace page","code":"const out = {};\nconst fonts = await figma.listAvailableFontsAsync();\nconst byFam = {};\nfor (const f of fonts) {\n  if (/^(Nunito|Inter)$/i.test(f.fontName.family)) {\n    (byFam[f.fontName.family] = byFam[f.fontName.family] || []).push(f.fontName.style);\n  }\n}\nout.fonts = byFam;\n\n// coin logo fill info\nconst btc = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('2:8');\nout.coinFill = btc.fills.map(f => ({ type: f.type, hash: f.imageHash, scale: f.scaleMode }));\n\n// button internals\nconst btn = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('3:19');\nout.button = {\n  layoutMode: btn.layoutMode,\n  primaryAxisAlignItems: btn.primaryAxisAlignItems,\n  counterAxisAlignItems: btn.counterAxisAlignItems,\n  itemSpacing: btn.itemSpacing,\n  padding: [btn.paddingTop, btn.paddingRight, btn.paddingBottom, btn.paddingLeft],\n  textStyleId: (await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('3:20')).textStyleId,\n};\nconst tf = await figma.getNodeByIdAsync('3:22');\nout.textfield = { layoutMode: tf.layoutMode, align: tf.counterAxisAlignItems, pad: [tf.paddingLeft, tf.paddingRight] };\n\n// workspace page state\nconst ws = figma.root.children.find(p => p.id === '4:2');\nout.workspace = { name: ws.name, children: ws.children.map(c => ({ id: c.id, name: c.name, type: c.type })) };\n\n// write test\nawait figma.setCurrentPageAsync(ws);\nawait figma.loadFontAsync({ family: 'Nunito', style: 'Bold' });\nconst t = figma.createFrame();\nt.name = '__write_test__';\nt.resize(100, 100);\nt.fills = [{ type: 'SOLID', color: { r: 1, g: 0, b: 0 } }];\nout.writeTest = { ok: true, id: t